            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "redbudval"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an excellent recipe. I have used it for several holidays and gotten rave reviews from my guests. Go easy on the hot sauce and let them add their own fire. Some serving suggestions: cook some medium shrimp and chill then on a long toothpick (I use cut in half bamboo skewers) add shrimp, cocktail onion and pimento olive or some other green olive (no black olives) and stick in cocktail glass then add vodka and BM mix...be prepared to be amazed.",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-23T13:46:51.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I spent the evening trying some other single serving recipies on this site. They were OK. I used the remainder of my big jug of tomato juice to make this stuff, and it was the bomb! The beef consume sets this apart from the pack. The only thing I changed was I used a half a tbsp of celery salt and a half tbsp of Old Bay Seasoning instead of all celery salt. I'm a huge Crystal Hot Sauce fan, so I used that instead of the Tobasco. You will not be disappointed.",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-15T19:41:17.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christopher Grimm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This mix turned out great. Much better than any store bought I've tried. I followed the recipe exact, but for two things. I used the whole 10 oz can of beef consumme and I added about 1/2 tbsp of ground horseradish. It was perfect to my taste and I will definitely use this recipe in the future.",
            "datePublished": "2019-11-10T17:13:46.517Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stixmodee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was in the bar business for 15 years and have made hundreds of Bloody Mary's. I had never heard of beef consommé'being used before, so I was intrigued by this recipe. It is fantastic! The perfect amount of spices and flavor. I did add a Tbs. of horseradish. Easy to make. Easier to drink!",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-10T12:25:08.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Turtlesr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I must edit my original review but I can't figure out how. So here is a second. We have found we like V8 in place of tomato juice. Spicey V8 or original. Always try oringinal recipe as intended then adjust to your personal liking. Either way this is a 5 star! Do NOT leave out the beef consumme'.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-15T17:15:35.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gini Blum Ruthven"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Used broth made with Better than Bouillon because I didn’t have consommé. Added a tsp of horseradish. Two thumbs up! Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-23T18:06:50.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great version of the classic Bloody Mary. Horseradish was never used . I didn't have a lemon so I used a lime.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-01T18:43:53.497Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jodi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Well I think it turned out pretty good. Thought I ran through all the ingredients and ran to the store to get lemon and horseradish. I didn't have celery salt so I use Old Bay which is a lot of celery salt so that was fine. Didn't have BBQ sauce so added extra Worcestershire. Had the Consomme. I didn't have a hot sauce so substituted Tabasco Chipotle sauce. Next time I want to follow the recipe with more of the actual ingredients. I did add an extra teaspoon of prepared horseradish. I could take it up a notch but I think this is a really good base and then customize it to your liking. Thank you. Much cheaper than buying store bought and then that's a crap shoot unless you spend a lot of money. Thank you, I will make this up for gatherings for sure.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-29T01:31:07.329Z"
          },
          {
